{number: 32}
{title: Jesus, Keep Me Near the Cross}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Jesus, keep me near the cross;
[F] There a precious [C] fountain,
Free to all, a healing stream,
Flows from [G7] Calvary's [C] mountain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
In the [C] cross, in the [F] cross,
[C] Be my glory [G7] ever,
Till my [C] raptured soul shall [F] find
[C] Rest be-[G7] yond the [C] river.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Near the cross, a trembling soul,
[F] Love and mercy [C] found me;
There the bright and morning star
Sheds its [G7] beams a-[C] round me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Near the cross! O Lamb of God,
[F] Bring its scenes be-[C] fore me;
Help me walk from day to day
With its [G7] shadow [C] o'er me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] Near the cross I'll watch and wait,
[F] Hoping, trusting [C] ever,
Till I reach the golden strand
Just be-[G7] yond the [C] river.
{end_of_verse}
